for tic,para in {
 '417917895':'Bounded depth check: same sector-15 event core medians are 131.30/127.68 ppt in QLP versus 105.16/101.90 ppt in the 3x3 extraction; the deepest-three estimates are 147.72/146.85 versus 117.92/116.99 ppt. Pixel 1x1, 3x3 and 5x5 core ranges are 101.67-107.81, 101.90-105.16 and 100.31-103.18 ppt. A real reduction-dependent difference remains after matching sector and estimator; its cause is not established. Both dips repeat with the correct timing, and the independent source check locates their deficit near the target rather than the capable neighbour. No equality of depths is assumed. See depth-sanity-417917895.json.',
 '162075402':'Bounded depth check in sector80: four matching primary epochs yield QLP core depths 123.73-126.43 ppt versus 97.84-99.23 ppt in the independent 3x3 extraction. Pixel 1x1 depths 106.81-112.03 and 5x5 depths 77.13-78.90 ppt establish aperture dependence in this crowded field; QLP deepest-three depths are 146.89-149.03 ppt. The TARS independent product gives 131.86 and 117.63 ppt with fixed QLP shapes; its QUALITY column is absent and the formal errors omit systematics. These are consistent repeated eclipses but not identical depth estimates; dilution and reduction differences remain characterization limitations. See depth-sanity-162075402.json. Primary period is 5.327672 d; a half-period alias can arise from secondary eclipses and does not replace the full primary repetition.',
 '156851362':'The two fitted QLP events span approximately four primary cycles. Five independently extracted pixel dips recover the approximately4.03 d repetition. The two-event photometric period has no fitted uncertainty; this is sufficient repetition evidence without a precise ephemeris claim.'}.items():
 p=B/f'TIC-{tic}.md';p.write_text(p.read_text()+'\n'+para+'\n',encoding='utf-8')
for tic in ['417917895','162075402']:
 (B/f'DEPTH-SANITY-{tic}.md').write_text(f'# TIC {tic} depth sanity\n\n'+next(p for t,p in {'417917895':'Same-sector QLP core depths 131.30/127.68 ppt versus 3x3 105.16/101.90 ppt; varying pixel apertures gives about100-108 ppt. Reduction-dependent difference persists; no cause established. Repeated dips and direct spatial attribution support the EB, with depth/dilution unresolved.','162075402':'Same-sector QLP core depths123.73-126.43 ppt versus3x3 97.84-99.23 ppt;1x1 106.81-112.03 and5x5 77.13-78.90 ppt show aperture dependence. TARS gives131.86/117.63 ppt, no QUALITY column. Source and timing evidence supports the target; no equality of depth or cause is claimed.'}.items() if t==tic)+'\n\nThe matching core estimator uses each predicted primary epoch and measured duration; pre/post local medians and QUALITY=0 where present. Counts, deep-three estimates, URI, identity and SHA256 are in depth-sanity-'+tic+'.json; code is depth_sanity.py. No formal uncertainty or dilution model is inferred.\n')
rows=list(csv.DictReader((B/'RESULTS.csv').open()));expected=[q['tic'] for q in csv.DictReader((B.parent/'queue.csv').open()) if q['batch']=='6'];assert [r['tic'] for r in rows]==expected and len(list(B.glob('TIC-*.md')))==10
